<div class="ptl_page"><div class="ptl_col_1"><div class="ptl_portlet_vertical"><div class="ptl_top_portlet" style="display:none;"></div><div id="ctl00_ContentPlaceHolder1_ctl12_divContent"><p>If you get a parking citation...<br>
<br>
You can pay the parking citation online: <a href="http://www.citationprocessingcenter.com/index.aspx" title="website opens in new window">Citation Processing Center</a><br>
If you have questions about the citation, you can call: 1 (800) 989-2058<br>
<br>
If you have received a parking citation, carefully read and follow all the instructions on the citation. Failure to submit payment within the required time may result in penalties being added to the original fine, holds being placed against your vehicle's registration. <br>
<br>
If you make a payment by mail, send the proper amount of penalty in check or money order. PLEASE DO NOT SEND CASH. <br>
<br>
Mail to: <br>
City of San Jacinto<br>
Citation Processing Center <br>
P.O. Box 10479 <br>
Newport Beach, CA 92658-0479<br>
<br>
*CITATION PAYMENT MUST BE MAILED TO THE ADDRESS ABOVE. WE DO NOT ACCEPT PAYMENTS IN PERSON OR MAILED TO CITY HALL*<br>
<br>
Credit card payment can be made by calling: 1(800)989-2058 or on the website www.CitationProcessingCenter.com.<br>
<br>
To Respond To The Citation:<br>
<br>
The registered owner of lessee of the vehicle cited shall within 21 days of issuance, either:<br>
<br>
</p>
<ul>
    <li>Pay the parking penalty</li>
    <li>Submit a written appeal online at www.CitationProcessingCenter.com or mail your appeal and your supporting documentation to the address noted above. Your payment or appeal must be received within 21 days of the of the citation date. Submitted documents will not be returned. </li>
</ul>
<p>Payment Plan Options:</p>
<ul>
    <li>(California State Legislature AB 503, AB 2544 "indigent"). Qualified indigents are eligible for special payment options. To qualify, please provide the information: <a href="/UserFiles/Servers/Server_10384345/File/City Government/Community Development/Parking/ProofOfIndigence0718.pdf" title="document opens in new window">Proof of Indigence</a>. Contact City Hall for help submitting your information at (951) 487-7330.</li>
</ul></div>
